# CoW 2G — mutating method on a TUPLE-FIELD receiver of a bare tuple param.
# `t.0.push(i)` root-peels through the tuple field to `t`; the prescan records
# `@mut:t.0` (via the TupleFieldAccess arm of extract_path_for_mut) so the
# loop-carried materialize of `t` fires. Expect the private copy's first field
# grows to 3 (1 + 2), caller stays 1.
#
# NOTE: only the RECEIVER shape is covered. A tuple-field ASSIGN target
# (`t.0 = v`) is a PRE-EXISTING silent no-op (lower_assign has no
# TupleFieldAccess arm) — see cow_loop_bare_param_tuple_assign.gg.
#
# In known_gaps/ (out of the runtime-diff corpus) pending the self-host CoW-2G
# mirror. Rust lane is correct.
void f((Vector[int], int) t):
    int i = 0
    while i < 2:
        t.0.push(i)
        i = i + 1
    print(t.0.len())

void main():
    (Vector[int], int) p = ([9], 0)
    f(p)
    print(p.0.len())
